 to forward stdin  To make the shell command a true bi-directional IO channel, we need it to support reading from stdin properly.  BUG=none TEST=manually  Change-Id: I8176fcf7adc931f5636a97460fb71cdafab9eedf Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323680 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rong Chang &lt;rongchang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323680" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/80/323680/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia3068528ceeded5c49f8ea905fb7cc8cedb22a1f" commit="593a6b0fbea5db98121abcfcb4677d2414180cda" commit_message="overlord: ghost: buffer handling of leftover data  When the overlord control channel switch into a data channel after registration, the leftover data need to be interpreted as input data steam. Instead of having to deal with the leftover separately, implement a wrapper class that supports 'UnRecv'. UnRecv push the data in to a buffer, which will later be consume with Recv() is called.  BUG=none TEST=`go/src/overlord/test/overlord_e2e_unittest.py`  Change-Id: Ia3068528ceeded5c49f8ea905fb7cc8cedb22a1f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323923 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rong Chang &lt;rongchang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323923" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/23/323923/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I1257118b4dc17bf78a8120ad2f44bb78b377805e" commit="a913af28932b9e0a208e8b986a7137c4bb7096fb" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm: panel: Fix auo_b101ean01 to use 66.667 pixel clock  The auo_b101ean01 info was all assuming that we could make a 72.5 MHz pixel clock.  We can't since we need to be sourced from either 400 MHz or 594 MHz.  That means we were actually using a 66.667 MHz pixel clock and getting a ~55 Hz refresh rate.  Let's adjust settings to give us something close to 60 Hz refresh rate (actually 59.45 Hz) while keeping a reasonable vblank and not specifying an &quot;impossible&quot; pixel clock.  BUG=chromium:571045 TEST=webgl aquarium 59-60 FPS now; touch works; ddrfreq works  Change-Id: I1257118b4dc17bf78a8120ad2f44bb78b377805e Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323211 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323211" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/11/323211/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia05a9978d267d21651afb71775abb06fbef99864" commit="fec2fdfff794dd5c625af0354d7ef593b9b36204" commit_message="pty_driver: fix pexpect version compatibility.  pexpect &lt;= 3.3 fdpexpect is a separate module; pexpect &gt; 3.3 fdpexpect is a submodule of pexpect. Make fdpexpect work for all versions.  BUG=none TEST=`sudo servod -b oak;       python -c &quot;import xmlrpclib;        xmlrpclib.Server('http://localhost:9999').ctrl_key()&quot;`  Change-Id: Ia05a9978d267d21651afb71775abb06fbef99864 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324701 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Anatol Pomazau &lt;anatol@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324701" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" ref="refs/changes/01/324701/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2ca1a1f52cf59e946cca0e1958648b0da068b456" commit="3a3fe2522bbc147ea55e1f915233a40c0a271c94" commit_message="Add amd64-generic-goofy builder configuration  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48492 TEST=None  Change-Id: I2ca1a1f52cf59e946cca0e1958648b0da068b456 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323812 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="323812" owner_email="bhthompson@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/12/323812/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Iaac892fa2aa98226b41ea0289468075f2f411a69" commit="7388285b55f004f71ecfe9bba4b4ac367ef02fac" commit_message="UPSTREAM: pinctrl: mediatek: mt8* make driver explicitly non-modular  The Kconfig for these drivers are currently:  config PINCTRL_MT8127         bool &quot;Mediatek MT8127 pin control&quot; if COMPILE_TEST &amp;&amp; !MACH_MT8127  config PINCTRL_MT8135         bool &quot;Mediatek MT8135 pin control&quot; if COMPILE_TEST &amp;&amp; !MACH_MT8135  config PINCTRL_MT8173         bool &quot;Mediatek MT8173 pin control&quot;  ...meaning that they are currently not being built as a module by anyone. Lets remove the modular code that is essentially orphaned, so that when reading the driver there is no doubt it is builtin-only.  A recent commit moved these from module_init to arch_initcall already, so the init ordering remains untouched with this commit.  We also delete the MODULE_LICENSE tag etc. since all that information is already contained at the top of the file in the comments.  Also note that MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE is a no-op for non-modular code.  Cc: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Cc: Matthias Brugger &lt;matthias.bgg@gmail.com&gt; Cc: Hongzhou Yang &lt;hongzhou.yang@mediatek.com&gt; Cc: Yingjoe Chen &lt;yingjoe.chen@mediatek.com&gt; Cc: linux-gpio@vger.kernel.org Cc: linux-mediatek@lists.infradead.org Signed-off-by: Paul Gortmaker &lt;paul.gortmaker@windriver.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Linus Walleij &lt;linus.walleij@linaro.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit cc301fd1fcf28f92b122f7f6105db9d7c182cccc  git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/linusw/linux-pinctrl for-next) Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48602 TEST=Build and boot oak-rev4 to UI  Change-Id: Iaac892fa2aa98226b41ea0289468075f2f411a69 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324742 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324742" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/42/324742/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ida3f43151c1b5febac2a441af31b09bb31be280d" commit="d39734519d144410e2f658e0cbb4bf1ff3572456" commit_message="oak: update INA219 overlay to match Rev5 board configuration.  (1) update power rails name (2) update sense resistors value  BUG=None TEST=Manually $ sudo emerge hdctools $ sudo servod -b oak -c oak.xml  Change-Id: Ida3f43151c1b5febac2a441af31b09bb31be280d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324679 Commit-Ready: Tony Lin &lt;tonycwlin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Tony Lin &lt;tonycwlin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324679" owner_email="tonycwlin@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" ref="refs/changes/79/324679/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I9c4fccaae27a966a3969ad2c806c073e0f89c5f7" commit="d9643e548120cc451cebcaa1cce0e1b6f656882a" commit_message="FROMLIST: dma-buf: Add ioctls to allow userspace to flush  The userspace might need some sort of cache coherency management e.g. when CPU and GPU domains are being accessed through dma-buf at the same time. To circumvent this problem there are begin/end coherency markers, that forward directly to existing dma-buf device drivers vfunc hooks. Userspace can make use of those markers through the DMA_BUF_IOCTL_SYNC ioctl. The sequence would be used like following:      - mmap dma-buf fd      - for each drawing/upload cycle in CPU 1. SYNC_START ioctl, 2. read/write        to mmap area 3. SYNC_END ioctl. This can be repeated as often as you        want (with the new data being consumed by the GPU or say scanout device)      - munmap once you don't need the buffer any more  v2 (Tiago): Fix header file type names (u64 -&gt; __u64) v3 (Tiago): Add documentation. Use enum dma_buf_sync_flags to the begin/end dma-buf functions. Check for overflows in start/length. v4 (Tiago): use 2d regions for sync. v5 (Tiago): forget about 2d regions (v4); use _IOW in DMA_BUF_IOCTL_SYNC and remove range information from struct dma_buf_sync. v6 (Tiago): use __u64 structured padded flags instead enum. Adjust documentation about the recommendation on using sync ioctls. v7 (Tiago): Alex' nit on flags definition and being even more wording in the doc about sync usage.  BUG=chromium:487189  Change-Id: I9c4fccaae27a966a3969ad2c806c073e0f89c5f7 Cc: Sumit Semwal &lt;sumit.semwal@linaro.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Tiago Vignatti &lt;tiago.vignatti@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/322183 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="322183" owner_email="tiago.vignatti@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/83/322183/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ib200ab2b0e316c7bfe03ae03f3e5eb953ec515eb" commit="083f53ff557dc34629524e24ba01df8df55125e4" commit_message="UPSTREAM: [media] media: New flag V4L2_CTRL_FLAG_EXECUTE_ON_WRITE  Create a new flag that represent controls which its value needs to be passed to the driver even if it has not changed.  They typically represent actions, like triggering a flash or clearing an error flag. So writing to such a control means some action is executed.  Signed-off-by: Ricardo Ribalda Delgado &lt;ricardo.ribalda@gmail.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Hans Verkuil &lt;hans.verkuil@cisco.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mauro Carvalho Chehab &lt;mchehab@osg.samsung.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit b6e5b8f1a90230f922de8af59cdaf1ad83e1ac1e) Signed-off-by: Wu-Cheng Li &lt;wuchengli@chromium.org&gt;  Conflicts:   include/uapi/linux/videodev2.h  BUG=chromium:572825 TEST=Play video on veyron_jerry.  Change-Id: Ib200ab2b0e316c7bfe03ae03f3e5eb953ec515eb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324872 Commit-Ready: Wu-cheng Li &lt;wuchengli@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wu-cheng Li &lt;wuchengli@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Heng-ruey Hsu &lt;henryhsu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324872" owner_email="wuchengli@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/72/324872/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7884.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>